petra 0

# Family: any Cu/PVC cable from 2.5 to 16 mm2, clipped direct, up to 20 m, drawing up
# to 13 A, in 10-40 degC ambient, stays at or below 70 degC and drops at most 3 % of
# 230 V. `petra certify-family` proves both claims over the whole box once (R4) and
# stores the partitions in the library. circuit_pass.petra (2.5 mm2, 18 m, 10 A) sits
# inside the box, so its two claims reuse these certificates.
#
# The hottest corner is 2.5 mm2 with 0.8 mm insulation, 13 A, 40 degC and the low
# surface coefficient h = 5 W/m2K, with the conductor at its IEC 60228 maximum
# resistance: about 68.8 degC. A 16 A draw would reach about 86.2 degC there, which is
# why the draw stops at 13 A (tests/test_library.py).

param size       in [2.5 mm2, 16 mm2]
param insulation in [0.8 mm, 1.0 mm]
param run        in [0 m, 20 m]

circuit c {
  supply mains voltage 230 V
  wire w1 cable cable.cu_pvc area param size insulation param insulation length param run install install.clipped_direct
  consumer load

  connect mains.out -> w1.a
  connect w1.b -> load.in
}
